Hermlet is an independent community project. It is not affiliated with,
endorsed by or supported by Nous Research. "Hermes", "Hermes Agent" and "Nous
Research" are names of Nous Research and are used here only to describe what
this software works with.

Where ideas came from
---------------------

* Muse Gadgets (https://github.com/facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk, Apache
  2.0) for the shape of the thing: a device SDK you install on a spare Linux
  box, with a README for people and an AGENTS.md for coding agents. No code
  from it is used.

* Hermes Gadget (https://github.com/Adolanium/hermes-gadget-sdk, MIT, by the
  Hermes Gadget SDK contributors) for how a device can plug into Hermes as a
  platform plugin. The optional plugin in plugin/ follows the same approach:
  each device is a direct-message chat, Hermes's own pairing codes approve it,
  a key enrolled on first contact is proven by HMAC afterwards, and binary
  WebSocket frames carry a four-byte channel/stream/sequence header. The code
  here was written for this project against the same Hermes interfaces.

